-- Regression test for lexical section scoping — FIX C (spec §5.5).
--
-- An IMPORTED binding and a local section binding that share a name AND a type
-- must remain a genuine ambiguity: the local section binding must NOT silently
-- shadow the import. `math` exports `EULER : NUMBER`; the local section here
-- also defines `EULER : NUMBER`. An unqualified reference to `EULER` is
-- therefore ambiguous and must raise an AmbiguousTermError, exactly as it did
-- before section-proximity scoping was introduced.

IMPORT math

§ `Local Section`
GIVETH A NUMBER
EULER MEANS 3

#EVAL EULER    -- AmbiguousTermError: local EULER vs math's EULER
